## PILLAR 4: PLAN — Staffing & Work Plan

### Before Contract Start, Sub Must Provide:

**Staffing Plan:**
- [ ] Names and roles of key personnel assigned to the contract
- [ ] Qualifications/certifications of each person (especially licensed roles)
- [ ] Backup personnel plan (who covers if someone is sick/unavailable?)
- [ ] Background check clearance (if federal facility access required)
- [ ] Training documentation (specific to service type)

**Work Plan:**
- [ ] How they will execute the scope of work — step by step
- [ ] Equipment and materials they will provide
- [ ] Quality control procedures
- [ ] What they need from DDI to perform (access, credentials, information)

**Timeline Alignment:**
- [ ] Sub's proposed schedule aligns with contract performance period
- [ ] Sub can meet all contract milestones and deadlines
- [ ] Ramp-up time accounted for (how quickly can they start after award?)
- [ ] Response time commitments (especially for on-call services like NEMT, snow removal)

### DDI's Role as Prime (What WE Manage):

- All communication with the Contracting Officer
- All contract reporting (monthly reports, invoicing, performance documentation)
- Quality assurance oversight
- Schedule management and milestone tracking
- Compliance with all contract terms and FAR/DFAR requirements
- Status updates to the CO on sub performance
- Issue resolution and escalation

**The sub executes. DDI manages. That's the split.**

