## CRITICAL REMINDERS

1. **YOU are responsible for the contract.** Not the sub. If the sub fails, your CPARS takes the hit, your past performance suffers, and your business reputation is damaged.

2. **It is illegal to be a pass-through.** DDI must actively manage the contract — scheduling, quality, reporting, CO communication. The sub provides labor/services. DDI provides management and oversight.

3. **The CO may never know the sub.** All communication with the government goes through DDI. The sub is invisible to the CO unless the contract specifically requires sub identification.

4. **NDA before information. Non-Compete before details. COI before work.** This is the order. Always.

5. **Document everything.** Every communication, every performance issue, every milestone. This protects DDI legally and builds the case for future proposals.

